ecessarily  thanked you for it because they still  would have descended on my channel  regardless but having been on the  receiving end of people who  did not do that no if it helps at all  it's worth doing  assuming you care that's kind of the  other thing  they have to actually care although  i should be clear it's not a risk-free  proposition  and not just from the corporate  element that i mentioned the sort of  let's not alienate fans  handling it wrong can turn the entire  thing  worse i think probably the best example  of that  is ghostbusters 2016. this was a reboot  that a lot of people  were not happy about i wasn't happy  about on principle just because it's a  reboot  and especially after seeing it and  honestly the movie's fine  it's fine but i was annoyed with it  because there's absolutely nothing about  it that required a continuity reset  there's nothing that needed to be a  reboot there was nothing going on with  that story  or characters or world or aesthetic that  required them to go  okay we're hitting the restart button  that thing before that is no longer  ghostbusters now  this is ghostbusters that rubbed me the  wrong way  but there were also a lot of people who  just got very very very angry because it  was all women  and were frankly sexist apples about it  i'm not gonna mince words i don't really  care about the feelings of people  who went that road however  in attempting to respond to that some of  the things that  the cast and crew did with things like  that  somewhat infamous now shot of them all  standing around with the sign that said  girl power  it didn't feel like condemning fan  behavior  it felt like poking the bear and the way  that  some of them would speak and i'm not  sure this was actually the intention  of any of the people involved in that  film who spoke out against that but it  it was interpreted this way and it  it wasn't difficult to interpret some of  it this way  it came across as anyone who is  saying that this is a bad idea or we  shouldn't be doing this  they're mad at us because it's all women  and speaking of someone who thought it  was a terrible idea but had no issue  with that like  don't let me in with the rest of them  please  so there is an argument to be made that  that  attempt to call out behavior of an  admittedly  damaging and toxic sliver of fandom  just made it feel like they were blaming  a much larger chunk of fandom than was  actually the problem and ended up  alienating more people  now that's incredibly hard to prove  in any meaningful way because i have no  way of knowing  what the box office or the support for  the film might have been if they had not  responded in that way  i can only speculate but that certainly  is the impression that i got left with  and if i  as a relative lay person came away from  that  i guarantee you that pretty much anybody  involved in the industry came away with  a similar if not much  uh more number and  uh money lost backed version of that  same  conclusion i think if i were gonna try  and come down  somewhere on this  the closest thing i'm going to come to a  hard line because i think ultimately all  this is incredibly situational and like  i said i don't have answers  but i think it is very difficult  for studios directors  you the face of youtube channels anybody  to try and regulate  the behavior of fans toward other fans  because that's just kind of stepping  into something that  only kind of involves you like it  involves your work  but you know is that really your place  to step  in because there's a fan war going on  uh i mean it i don't think it would hurt  every now and then for somebody to  somebody with like creative authority  as opposed to like a studio head because  nobody cares what they think  as far as public statements go and they  know that that's why they don't say  things  but for somebody with uh with a creative  stake in creative clout in the project  to go hey  you know i understand you you all care  you're passionate but  folks you need to you need to take a  breath and and calm down a little  because this is supposed to be fun  for everyone involved i don't think you  can really go too wrong just  having somebody say that now again if  they need to  i do however feel increasingly that  studios especially but even  directors  or the people who run these projects  manage these ips  they do have a responsibility to their  own employees so when i look back  at something like what happened with the  fifth harry potter  and what happened to katie liang  and the fact that warner brothers told  her to basically suck it up and not talk  about it  instead of protecting a child  a young teenager who  they hired and then  refused to help or assist  or protect no  that's not okay  these people work for you  you are making money off their back  off of their work the least you could do  is have their back  and not just throw them to rabid fans  to be torn apart in social media to the  point that they have to quit  various social media platforms which  happens  frighteningly often now i do feel a need  to clarify  i'm a little bit more iffy if fans are  coming at a  it's usually an actor but somebody  involved in a project  for something that they did that has  nothing to do with that project  that's probably not something you want  to step in  but when you're basically dealing with  people who are  employed by you brought into this world  by you  who are being harassed simply  by existing and in many cases  just by existing as someone who isn't  cis  male white and heterosexual  uh yeah no don't don't leave them out to  dry  and just whoever you are  if you're a youtuber if you have a  notable twitter following  if you are a director if you run a  studio  realize that what you put out  in the world can  and will drive people's  actions people will  do things to other people  based off things that you tell them  that doesn't mean you have control over  over them they still are deciding to do  these things that on their own  but if you're on a youtube channel  and you decide to do a takedown video of  somebody  you are unleashing your fan base at them  whether you appreciate that or not it is  what you're doing and if you run a  studio  and you're casting a major franchise  film that people care a lot about  anyone who you cast in a role is going  to be in the crosshairs potentially of a  lot of people  and if you're gonna bring them in into  that situation  you owe it to them  to try and protect them and try and  wrangle those fans  if you can and again the ability to do  so is very limited  but i think how many people were  pleasantly surprised by zack snyder  calling out a sliver of fandom  that he took issue with and he felt was  not in the spirit of what he wanted his  work to represent  part of why that's notable is because of  how rare it is  and maybe it shouldn't be that rare  i know it's scary i know it is  no easy thing and i  certainly for one hope i never have to  do it  i don't ever want to have to distance  myself from people who've supported me  but i'd like to think if it ever comes  to it  i'll do it if i have to being in the  public eye producing consumption  intended for the largest participle  audience  is not easy  it's draining it's exhausting  and thinking about how many people your  work is impacting if you have a  substantial following  or your work uh brings a particularly  devoted fan base  that's an intimidating thing to think  about  but you still need to think about it  or at least maybe if you're large enough  hire somebody  to think about it that's what pr  management's for  but yeah i guess i'm going to wrap it up  there  i feel like there is some degree of  responsibility but i  can't draw a line on where that is  and whose precise responsibility it is  in specific situations  but when fans run  rampant in the name of love for  a property or personality  and the people behind that property or  personality  remain silent it's a tacit endorsement  you're not saying they should stop  and you probably should those are my  rambling thoughts on all this  what do you think about this topic in  general it's a difficult one to try and  get fully on top of and i'm certainly  interested to hear what you have to say  just do it politely whatever your  thoughts are drop them down in the  comments and let's talk about it  i have a patreon and that is how i am  able to do this  without the support of my patreon  backers i would not  be able to cover my bills this is in  fact my entire living at this point  any amount you're able to support is of  great assistance and there are rewards  for every tier  from being able to see the docket early  to getting to vote on  topics to a patreon exclusive discord to  getting your name in the credits which  you'll be seeing  shortly but even if you can't do that  like share subscribe  the bell hey if you're feeling ambitious  those all help me out as well  keeps the algorithm from completely  forgetting me  but i'm not gonna tell you even have to  do that  because while i do feel a certain amount  of responsibility  at the end of the day you  are the council and i'm just running the  meetings  to the best of my ability and until next  time  this council is adjourned  [Music]  um  [Music]  [Applause]  hmm  [Music]  [Music]  um
 

